        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>I know that it's probably way too late, but the way I would've handled it was to have them roll an Overcome for disposing of the bomb, with the mandate that any resulting Twist would be a story twist for later.&nbsp; That way the players feel like they still have agency, and the players (though not the characters) get foreshadowing as far as how annoying the consequences should be.&nbsp; Plus it gives you some kind of guideline for how annoying to make said consequences!</p>\r\n\r\n<p>I think the already mentioned suggestions of having the blast just so happen to further destabalize the russian power plant (again, to what degree being based on Twist severity) is the best way to go here.</p>",
